*Brandon Brown, former senior vice president of institutional advancement at [[Paine College]] and nominee for {{ushr|SC|4}} in [[2004 United States House of Representatives elections in South Carolina#District 4|2004]] and [[2018 United States House of Representatives elections in South Carolina#District 4|2018]]<ref>{{cite news |last1=Quinn |first1=Abigail |title=Brandon Brown to challenge Lindsey Graham for South Carolina Senate seat |url=https://abcnews4.com/news/local/brandon-brown-to-challenge-lindsey-graham-for-south-carolina-senate-seat-wciv-abc-news-4-2025-local-politics-medicaid-rural-farmers-history-public-services-policies-working-middle-class-families-small-businesses-tariffs-quality-of-life-for-seniors |access-date=July 9, 2025 |publisher=[[WCIV]] |date=July 9, 2025 |language=en}}</ref><ref name="tsm30" />
